WEBVTT

00:03.450 --> 00:06.770
They told you about me because you 
couldn't afford their fees, right?

00:07.320 --> 00:11.380
Sure, it's fine. I'm not 
doing this just for money.

00:13.070 --> 00:14.110
Oh, me?

00:14.960 --> 00:16.950
You can just call me the Guide.

00:18.280 --> 00:23.330
I see. So, simply put, you're looking 
to hire someone to get revenge for you.

00:23.640 --> 00:26.920
And not just on one person, 
but also on his associates.

00:27.560 --> 00:29.050
Could you tell me why?

00:30.870 --> 00:33.340
Yes, I do need to know.

00:33.780 --> 00:38.160
The folks at the Underground Guild aren't 
particular as long as they get paid,

00:38.160 --> 00:40.390
but I put a lot of value on motivation.

00:42.640 --> 00:45.810
If you don't want to discuss it, 
we'll just say the deal fell through.

00:48.730 --> 00:50.440
You changed your mind, then?

00:52.000 --> 00:55.350
Well, that's certainly selfish!

00:55.350 --> 00:58.420
It's not even revenge. You're just
taking your frustrations out on him!

00:58.420 --> 01:00.410
You probably don't have any friends, do you?

01:00.850 --> 01:03.910
But you know, I like that.

01:04.520 --> 01:06.710
Very well. I'm willing to help.

01:07.080 --> 01:12.060
I've been working on this lately, and you've 
provided the perfect chance to test it.

01:12.660 --> 01:15.880
And I'll be able to fulfill 
your request at the same time.

01:16.290 --> 01:19.760
Now, would you mind telling me your name?

03:11.250 --> 03:13.360
That's a golem?

03:13.360 --> 03:14.670
It's inexplicable.

03:14.940 --> 03:17.600
You scared me! I guess you came out, too?

03:17.600 --> 03:19.900
My curiosity got the better of me.

03:19.900 --> 03:23.180
How could an ancient relic 
have possibly ended up here?

03:23.440 --> 03:24.450
And Lily?

03:24.450 --> 03:25.740
Still asleep.

03:25.740 --> 03:28.560
If she saw that monstrosity, 
it'd give her nightmares.

03:28.560 --> 03:30.280
It's for the best.

03:30.280 --> 03:31.690
Doc!

03:31.690 --> 03:34.200
Good to see you guys are all right.

03:34.200 --> 03:37.520
What a relief. We were on our way to get you.

03:37.520 --> 03:39.650
We're fine, but...

03:40.120 --> 03:43.280
Many of Lynga's werewolves are 
hurt so bad, they can't move.

03:46.030 --> 03:49.710
About half of the orcs are 
seriously injured, as well.

03:49.710 --> 03:51.790
What in the world is that creature?

03:52.080 --> 03:55.170
Even I can't eat all of that.

03:55.660 --> 03:57.430
Just calm down, you three.

03:57.430 --> 04:00.620
It seems to be some kind of artificial 
lifeform from a long time ago.

04:00.620 --> 04:03.140
Sorcery that was thought to be lost.

04:03.140 --> 04:05.180
Do you know where it came from?

04:05.180 --> 04:10.430
I do not. One of my orcs said they saw 
it coming from deeper in the slums.

04:10.840 --> 04:12.700
<i>Deeper in the slums?</i>

04:13.270 --> 04:15.290
<i>Could it be the Underground Guild?</i>

04:15.290 --> 04:17.980
<i>No, now's not the time to speculate.</i>

04:18.540 --> 04:21.090
Zophia, Lynga, Loewe.

04:21.090 --> 04:24.240
I need you all to work together 
and gather the injured in one spot.

04:26.990 --> 04:30.590
Whoever's responsible for this is 
gonna pay a hefty price. Count on it.

04:33.920 --> 04:39.180
As destructive as I had anticipated, 
but not quite as mobile.

04:39.180 --> 04:41.500
Looks like there's room for improvement.

04:42.080 --> 04:45.380
Still, it should be able 
to handle this request.

04:46.420 --> 04:52.640
I wonder how Zenos will react when the 
people who admire him start dying one by one.

04:53.350 --> 04:55.810
The curtain is rising on the first act.

04:55.810 --> 04:58.150
Put on a good show for me.

04:58.890 --> 05:00.650
Carry them over here!

05:00.650 --> 05:03.400
Follow the scent of blood 
to track down the injured!

05:03.400 --> 05:05.940
It's only five people! 
You can carry that many at once!

05:05.940 --> 05:07.910
Show them what orc strength looks like!

05:07.910 --> 05:10.180
You'll want to get clear, Carmilla.

05:13.110 --> 05:14.410
High Heal!

05:17.780 --> 05:19.790
Once you're healed, evacuate immediately!

05:23.040 --> 05:24.420
Damn it all...

05:24.700 --> 05:26.660
What are you so upset about?

05:26.660 --> 05:28.800
Imagine being dragged 
out in the dead of night

05:28.800 --> 05:31.060
and having to heal hundreds of people.

05:31.060 --> 05:34.930
There's no guarantee I'll get paid, and I'm 
worried about Lily. She's still at the house.

05:35.430 --> 05:37.310
I'm pissed at whoever's behind this!

05:37.310 --> 05:40.940
There's no telling what the 
golem's master was after,

05:40.940 --> 05:45.610
but I doubt they expected to have their 
aims thwarted under a cloud of griping.

05:45.610 --> 05:48.010
Well, this was unexpected.

05:48.010 --> 05:51.490
He's elite-class... maybe 
even better than that.

05:51.490 --> 05:56.160
Very good, Zenos. I love it when 
people exceed my expectations.

05:56.160 --> 05:59.260
That said, even if you heal the wounded,

05:59.260 --> 06:03.840
until you stop the golem, 
it's not a real solution.

06:03.840 --> 06:05.410
So what will you do?

06:06.240 --> 06:09.180
I'll concede the first round to you.

06:09.180 --> 06:11.970
But how will the second go?

06:12.880 --> 06:15.260
There are no more injured to be found.

06:15.260 --> 06:18.020
Lynga's men said the same thing.

06:18.020 --> 06:19.650
Likewise from the orcs.

06:20.620 --> 06:23.110
I see. Good work, everyone.

06:23.380 --> 06:26.740
Looks like no one died, thanks to you, Doc.

06:27.110 --> 06:28.630
That's a relief.

06:29.250 --> 06:31.240
But that thing is still making a mess...

06:31.240 --> 06:35.240
You don't suppose it'll get bored 
eventually and go home, do you?

06:35.240 --> 06:37.250
Impossible.

06:37.250 --> 06:41.010
Golems don't stop until they've 
fulfilled their orders.

06:41.010 --> 06:46.590
And I'd wager its orders were 
something like "destroy the slums."

06:46.590 --> 06:50.510
Aw, man, isn't this enough already?

06:50.920 --> 06:53.140
But it doesn't make sense.

06:53.140 --> 06:56.330
The high-purity magic stone 
that forms the core of golems

06:56.330 --> 06:59.930
is only found on the southernmost continent, 
where the Demon Lord's castle was.

06:59.930 --> 07:04.060
And it should have been mostly 
used up during the Man-Fiend War...

07:04.060 --> 07:07.170
The systems for black magic 
were thought lost for ages.

07:07.170 --> 07:10.610
Even the other ingredients for 
that hulk would be hard to acquire.

07:10.610 --> 07:12.050
Who could have done this?

07:12.500 --> 07:15.840
Well, we're looking right at the result, 
so what choice is there?

07:15.840 --> 07:18.870
This is a massive pain in the ass, 
but I guess I'd better go.

07:18.870 --> 07:20.960
Go? Go where?

07:21.480 --> 07:23.080
Isn't it obvious?

07:23.080 --> 07:25.210
I need to take down that monster.

07:26.830 --> 07:29.170
We're with you, Doc.

07:29.170 --> 07:32.680
You sure? I can't guarantee emergency care.

07:32.680 --> 07:36.240
I'm not about to stand around 
after this thing wrecked my home.

07:36.240 --> 07:38.100
This is our town!

07:38.100 --> 07:41.560
I say we teach this creature 
how fearsome we can be.

07:43.100 --> 07:46.370
Carmilla, how do we take down the golem?

07:46.370 --> 07:49.690
You must destroy the magic 
stone that makes up its core.

07:50.220 --> 07:53.070
Until you do, it'll simply 
regenerate, time and time again.

07:53.070 --> 07:55.210
<i>Destroy it, huh?</i>

07:55.210 --> 07:58.950
<i>If we destroy that magic stone, 
I doubt I'll be able to resell it.</i>

07:58.950 --> 08:02.830
All right, guys, start by hitting 
it with everything you've got.

08:02.830 --> 08:05.310
Don't worry. I'll back you up.

08:06.560 --> 08:08.060
Agility Boost.

08:10.070 --> 08:11.220
What the...

08:11.520 --> 08:13.500
I'm suddenly feeling light on my feet!

08:13.500 --> 08:15.590
Sir Zenos must've done something!

08:15.590 --> 08:18.220
Good. Now we can put up a real fight.

08:18.680 --> 08:21.730
Strength Boost. Impact Increase.

08:37.010 --> 08:38.990
Lynga! You alive?

08:39.550 --> 08:42.200
Surprisingly, yes.

08:42.200 --> 08:44.080
I think I have Sir Zenos to thank.

08:44.530 --> 08:47.830
I haven't done battle in a while, but 
I'm starting to remember how it works.

08:48.280 --> 08:50.920
<i>There are two things to watch out for.</i>

08:50.920 --> 08:53.970
<i>First, the farther away I am, 
the weaker the effects of magic become,</i>

08:53.970 --> 08:55.840
<i>so I need to maintain a certain distance.</i>

08:56.450 --> 08:59.600
<i>And the other... Healing, 
defense, and ability boosts</i>

08:59.600 --> 09:02.350
<i>might be similar, 
but their activation is distinct,</i>

09:02.350 --> 09:04.850
<i>so I can't functionally 
cast them all at once.</i>

09:05.450 --> 09:08.810
<i>I have to protect them until they go 
on the attack, then enhance that,</i>

09:09.200 --> 09:12.070
<i>and immediately heal any injuries they get.</i>

09:15.420 --> 09:17.950
Okay. I think I know what to do.

09:17.950 --> 09:21.100
It takes a certain amount 
of time to regenerate.

09:21.100 --> 09:23.950
I need you all to shatter both its legs!

09:24.260 --> 09:27.830
Never saw the day I'd be 
fighting alongside you girls!

09:29.330 --> 09:31.340
And it's all thanks to Sir Zenos!

09:31.340 --> 09:35.090
Can't say I've ever fought 
with two more reliable allies!

09:38.060 --> 09:39.970
Trouble, Doc! There's a kid over there!

09:39.970 --> 09:41.020
What?!

09:41.970 --> 09:43.680
<i>Did they not evacuate in time?</i>

09:43.680 --> 09:46.640
<i>Defense magic requires too much precision 
to cast on someone I can't see!</i>

09:46.640 --> 09:48.020
<i>Will I make it?!</i>

10:06.140 --> 10:11.080
My, my. You really are full of surprises, Zenos.

10:11.080 --> 10:13.820
You've claimed victory in the second act, too.

10:15.070 --> 10:18.130
And now it's time for the climax.

10:18.130 --> 10:21.150
One last decision awaits you.

10:21.680 --> 10:22.990
Inconceivable!

10:22.990 --> 10:26.890
Golems only follow simple orders. 
They shouldn't be capable of this!

10:26.890 --> 10:31.250
It's strange enough that it became 
fiercer once it started fighting you!

10:32.480 --> 10:36.740
Suppose someone was trying to create 
life from an imperfect magic stone.

10:36.740 --> 10:38.390
What options would they have?

10:40.470 --> 10:41.620
Are you saying...

10:41.620 --> 10:43.710
I've finished scanning the golem.

10:44.210 --> 10:46.090
The magic stone is in its left breast.

10:46.930 --> 10:50.060
Is that you in there, Aston?

10:52.340 --> 10:54.540
Would you mind telling me your name?

10:57.240 --> 11:00.820
I see. Aston, then.

11:03.900 --> 11:06.100
It looks like he's caught on.

11:06.100 --> 11:09.010
I thought the best way to create life

11:09.010 --> 11:12.600
from an imperfect magic stone would
be to combine it with a living human.

11:12.900 --> 11:17.150
The fusion of magic stone and 
man creates a new kind of core.

11:17.150 --> 11:20.490
And humans are hard to control, 
with their complex emotions,

11:20.490 --> 11:24.070
so a simpleton with intense negative 
feelings made the perfect choice.

11:24.610 --> 11:29.130
Beyond that, I just made it clear that the 
magic stone was necessary for his revenge,

11:29.130 --> 11:31.660
and once it was implanted, 
I created the golem.

11:32.210 --> 11:34.920
He and the magic stone are one now.

11:34.920 --> 11:40.260
So, how will you lower the 
curtain on this fight, Zenos?

11:40.650 --> 11:43.890
After all the lives you've healed and saved,

11:43.890 --> 11:46.660
you'll be killing the party member

11:46.660 --> 11:50.520
who lifted you out of the slums in order to destroy the magic stone!

11:51.150 --> 11:53.900
Could there be a more thrilling screenplay?!

11:54.360 --> 11:58.290
And all it cost me was one worthless life.

12:01.200 --> 12:04.160
All right, sorry, but I need the 
three of you to get clear.

12:04.430 --> 12:07.680
Doc? If we leave now, the thing's 
just gonna regenerate again.

12:07.680 --> 12:09.540
Lynga can still fight!

12:09.540 --> 12:11.760
We can handle the front line.

12:11.760 --> 12:14.710
That'd probably be the smarter idea, but...

12:15.680 --> 12:18.270
<i>"Healers shouldn't fight on the front lines."</i>

12:18.270 --> 12:21.670
<i>That was probably my teacher's 
seventh most repeated line.</i>

12:21.670 --> 12:23.800
<i>If you're focused on your own fight,</i>

12:23.800 --> 12:26.140
<i>you can't focus on supporting your allies.</i>

12:27.440 --> 12:28.680
<i>But...</i>

12:29.730 --> 12:33.310
Given what I know now, I'm the only 
one who can settle this with him.

12:39.350 --> 12:44.070
It's nearly dawn, and as I'm no fan 
of the sun, I'll be heading home.

12:44.390 --> 12:46.700
Okay. I should be home soon.

12:46.700 --> 12:48.830
I wasn't concerned in the first place,

12:48.830 --> 12:51.080
but I'll have some tea waiting for you.

12:51.080 --> 12:53.080
You make it sound like I'm gonna owe you,

12:53.080 --> 12:55.260
but I'm pretty sure it'll be Lily who makes it.

13:00.550 --> 13:04.050
Aston. It's just the two of us here now.

13:04.370 --> 13:07.140
When you called out to 
me here in the slums...

13:07.140 --> 13:09.460
That was where it all began, wasn't it?

13:10.180 --> 13:16.310
Someone as obnoxious and selfish as you, 
saving a kid? That's definitely odd.

13:16.310 --> 13:20.940
I heard Guile mention once that the reason 
you're obsessed with money and power is

13:20.940 --> 13:24.950
because your younger sister died when you 
couldn't afford the medicine she needed.

13:25.380 --> 13:28.770
Did that kid remind you of her?

13:28.770 --> 13:31.080
Is there still some part of 
your humanity in there?

13:33.070 --> 13:35.520
I guess the rage is still there, too.

13:35.520 --> 13:38.960
Angry because the pup you took in 
found a new home after you dumped him?

13:38.960 --> 13:43.780
Back then, I always thought it was strange 
how you knew I had no place to belong.

13:44.690 --> 13:46.440
But now I understand.

13:46.440 --> 13:48.470
It's because you didn't, either.

13:54.930 --> 13:59.310
Not that I really care at this point!

14:16.650 --> 14:18.580
Well, we meet again.

14:19.040 --> 14:21.330
Not that I'm thrilled about that...

14:21.640 --> 14:24.550
But today will be the last time 
I ever have to see your face.

14:28.550 --> 14:33.260
Now, it's time for our adventure 
to come to an end, Aston.

14:34.430 --> 14:37.580
Well. So that's his move?

14:37.580 --> 14:40.370
He kills with less hesitation 
than I expected.

14:40.370 --> 14:43.710
Then again, given the abuse 
he's apparently suffered,

14:43.710 --> 14:45.600
I suppose it's only natural.

14:46.390 --> 14:48.840
I guess that's a wrap, then.

14:49.660 --> 14:53.660
Kind of a disappointment, 
but it is what it is.

14:55.270 --> 14:56.410
Wait, no...

14:56.910 --> 14:58.040
Is he...

15:10.950 --> 15:14.140
This is exhausting enough. 
Settle down already!

15:14.140 --> 15:16.770
Healing and destroying in tandem?

15:16.770 --> 15:19.390
He cuts the parts that are 
fused with magic stone away,

15:19.390 --> 15:24.150
then gradually heals the bits 
of physiology that are left.

15:24.150 --> 15:26.780
Cut away too much and Aston dies.

15:26.780 --> 15:31.910
Hesitate too much and the magic stone 
will fuse with the regenerated body.

15:32.500 --> 15:34.120
And this is after healing hundreds,

15:34.120 --> 15:36.310
and having supported the 
demihumans in combat...

15:36.310 --> 15:42.660
Despite all that, he's maintaining all of his 
caution and focus to excise the magic stone?

15:43.720 --> 15:46.540
There's someone capable of doing all that?

15:47.020 --> 15:48.510
I can't believe what I'm seeing.

15:50.640 --> 15:55.840
To be honest, the world would 
probably be better off without you.

15:55.840 --> 15:57.890
I know I would be.

15:57.890 --> 15:59.820
Why?

16:01.490 --> 16:04.480
Do you realize how much all 
this damage is gonna cost you?

16:04.480 --> 16:08.700
And you're too broke to pay it off, so it'll 
be collected from your collaborator, too.

16:08.700 --> 16:11.530
You don't get to die until you 
confess who put you up to this.

16:12.010 --> 16:13.830
That's the first reason.

16:14.550 --> 16:18.220
As for the second... You might 
be a worthless piece of crap,

16:18.220 --> 16:22.160
but you did do two good things for me.

16:22.850 --> 16:27.230
You took me out of the slums, and you gave 
me that bit of severance pay on a whim.

16:28.630 --> 16:33.840
That single gold coin let me save Lily, 
which led to me starting the clinic,

16:33.840 --> 16:35.760
and that changed my life.

16:36.320 --> 16:37.760
There's one other thing...

16:37.760 --> 16:41.270
And it's the biggest reason I'm not going 
to just kill you to get this over with.

16:41.650 --> 16:44.020
It's because I'm a healer.

16:45.650 --> 16:50.280
You get it now, you stupid idiot?!

17:09.140 --> 17:14.510
It's now so clear to me how amazing 
you are that it makes me sick.

17:14.970 --> 17:19.260
I've lost everything, but you 
still expect me to go on living.

17:19.830 --> 17:22.770
Is this your revenge?

17:23.300 --> 17:26.140
Don't exaggerate. I didn't 
think it through that far.

17:29.150 --> 17:32.410
Through my haze, I could see you 
backing up the demihumans.

17:33.460 --> 17:36.530
You did the same thing with us, didn't you?

17:36.530 --> 17:38.580
You're creeping me out.

17:38.580 --> 17:40.310
What are you after now?

17:40.310 --> 17:44.910
That's harsh... but I guess I can't 
blame you for feeling that way.

17:45.450 --> 17:50.490
I spent my whole life using others, 
only to be used in the end.

17:50.490 --> 17:51.920
What a joke.

17:53.890 --> 17:58.650
I know nothing I say will make a 
difference, but I still need to say it.

17:59.140 --> 18:00.260
I'm sorry.

18:00.520 --> 18:02.320
I'm sorry, Zenos!

18:04.480 --> 18:07.520
That's enough. Chin up, Aston.

18:07.520 --> 18:09.570
How am I supposed to hit you otherwise?

18:07.520 --> 18:10.520
No! I can't accept that—

18:11.870 --> 18:15.780
Now that you're back to normal, I don't 
need to hold back anymore, y'know?

18:16.160 --> 18:19.160
Ability Boost. Ten times arm strength.

18:19.580 --> 18:22.780
I left just enough mana to pull this off.

18:20.570 --> 18:22.780
Whoa, hold on...

18:23.370 --> 18:25.660
The biggest reason I left you alive

18:25.940 --> 18:30.810
is because I wouldn't feel any better 
slugging you if you weren't conscious.

18:25.940 --> 18:30.810
Now, let's not be hasty... Hang on!

18:31.400 --> 18:34.250
Do you realize how much trouble 
you caused, you piece of crap?!

18:34.250 --> 18:37.290
I'm not letting you get off with an apology!

18:49.190 --> 18:50.510
Wake up already.

18:54.450 --> 18:57.590
I came because there were 
reports of a monster attack,

18:57.590 --> 18:59.650
and this is the second 
time I've encountered you.

19:00.100 --> 19:02.850
It took some gall to flee 
the way you did last time.

19:02.850 --> 19:04.530
Where's Zenos?

19:04.880 --> 19:07.920
I ran into him on the way 
here, and he filled me in.

19:07.920 --> 19:12.290
It's a miracle that a disaster of this 
scale happened without a single fatality.

19:12.680 --> 19:15.260
You'll owe Mr. Zenos for the rest of your life.

19:15.850 --> 19:17.950
I guess you're right.

19:19.470 --> 19:21.010
Aston Boehringal.

19:21.010 --> 19:24.570
You're under arrest for attempted assault,
fleeing arrest, false testimony,

19:24.570 --> 19:27.120
revenge-by-proxy, 
indiscriminate rampaging,

19:27.120 --> 19:31.520
damage of personal property, 
and many more charges.

19:31.520 --> 19:33.900
Brace yourself for a suitable punishment.

19:36.400 --> 19:39.740
I think I'll add public 
indecency to the list, too.

19:43.030 --> 19:45.840
Mr. Zenos had a message for you, as well.

19:46.450 --> 19:49.830
"I took your sword while 
you were unconscious."

19:49.830 --> 19:53.580
"It's a top-class item from an underground 
labyrinth, so it should sell for a decent price."

19:54.090 --> 19:57.420
"If nothing else, it should cover the 
cost of the damaged housewares."

19:57.420 --> 20:00.410
"And considering I was the one who found it,

20:00.410 --> 20:03.590
it's about time you gave it back,
you thief," he concluded.

20:05.010 --> 20:06.300
Now I...

20:07.330 --> 20:10.310
I really have lost everything.

20:10.720 --> 20:13.940
I don't have a single thing left.

20:14.880 --> 20:18.270
He mentioned one other thing.

20:18.270 --> 20:23.820
"That's your severance pay. I never want 
anything to do with you again," he said.

20:24.120 --> 20:25.510
Zenos!

20:39.380 --> 20:41.520
I feel like I'm gonna 
collapse from exhaustion.

20:41.520 --> 20:43.520
Doc, are you all right?

20:43.520 --> 20:46.500
Sir Zenos, you don't look so good!

20:46.500 --> 20:49.060
You're walking less and less steadily...

20:49.060 --> 20:50.480
Let me help you.

20:50.480 --> 20:53.690
It's fine. You're all probably just as tired.

20:57.320 --> 20:58.520
H-Hey!

20:58.880 --> 21:00.770
Don't sweat it, Doc.

21:00.770 --> 21:05.330
You look after me all the time, 
so it's only fair that I pay you back.

21:05.330 --> 21:09.760
It's only natural! Lynga would 
honestly prefer to get even closer.

21:10.400 --> 21:13.940
I won't let you two get ahead of me! 
I'll be the one doing any clinging.

21:15.670 --> 21:17.010
I was carrying him first!

21:16.200 --> 21:18.310
<i>Just this once, I'll indulge them.</i>

21:17.010 --> 21:18.880
She who gets in, gets the win!

21:18.880 --> 21:19.670
Say what?!

21:20.650 --> 21:23.170
I should go into hiding for a while.

21:24.070 --> 21:27.790
I'm sure you'll get in my 
way again someday, Zenos.

21:28.550 --> 21:30.940
When that happens, we'll play some more.

21:31.420 --> 21:33.340
I'm not going to forget you.

21:38.400 --> 21:41.270
Looks like you're alive. Resilient, aren't you?

21:41.270 --> 21:43.570
Sorry to disappoint you.

21:43.570 --> 21:45.240
You ought to be.

21:45.240 --> 21:49.000
I was looking forward to having 
peace and quiet again.

21:49.000 --> 21:53.750
She says that, but Carmilla was so 
worried about you being out late,

21:53.750 --> 21:56.300
she was floating all over the house!

21:56.300 --> 21:57.580
Foolish Lily!

21:57.580 --> 21:59.020
She's lying!

21:59.020 --> 22:00.050
Oh, yeah?

22:00.050 --> 22:02.210
Wh-What is that face supposed to mean?!

22:02.490 --> 22:06.300
I was worried when she 
told me what was going on,

22:06.300 --> 22:08.910
but I knew you'd make it back.

22:10.090 --> 22:12.060
Welcome home, Zenos!

22:17.550 --> 22:19.310
I'm back, everyone.

22:21.620 --> 22:23.340
Let's drink tea together!

23:55.580 --> 24:00.040
Special Service

23:57.260 --> 23:58.700
"Special Service."
